  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A heavy plank of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> hangs on three vertical wires of equal length arranged symmetrically (see figure). All the wires have the same cross-section. The middle wire is of steel and the other two are of copper. The modulus of elasticity of steel is assumed to be double that of copper. Determine the tensions in the wire. ( use&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;)<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0012_d195914a42f8.jpg\" style=\"width: 310px; height: 216px;\" /></p>\r"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi>cu</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>245</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi>steel</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>490</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi>cu</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>235</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi>steel</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>490</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>",
